            <ArticleTitle>Chronic pain control by means of an epidural catheter: report of a case with description of the method.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>903-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The feasibility of long-term epidural catheterization for control of chronic pain from sacral metastases has been demonstrated. Infection was not a problem and obstruction of the catheter did not occur. The short duration of action of currently available drugs was the major limitation of the technique. The technique described merits further investigation as an alternative to currently available methods.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
